agents.prompt:
You are adding connected wallet support to the escrow contract payment flow in `src/lib/components/bidding/ExternalWalletPaymentScreen.svelte`.

## Current State
ExternalWalletPaymentScreen shows a payment screen for escrow contracts. It:
- Displays a QR code and payment address for Lightning or Liquid escrow payments
- The user manually copies the address and sends BTC from their external wallet
- Props: `bid`, `taskTitle`, `escrowDetails` (paymentMethod, address, qrCode), `btcPrice`, callbacks
- Currently has no connected wallet integration

## What to Add

### Add a "Pay from connected wallet" option
When the feature flag is enabled and connected wallets exist, add a section below the QR code that lets the user pay directly from a connected wallet instead of manually copying the address.

### 1. Imports
```
import { connectedWalletsStore } from '$lib/stores/connected-wallets.store';
import { connectorRegistry } from '$lib/services/external-wallet/connector-registry';
import { FeatureFlagService, FEATURE_FLAGS } from '$lib/services/kill-switch';
import { EVMSignerNotAvailableError } from '$lib/services/external-wallet/types';
```

### 2. State
```
let selectedPayerWallet = $state<string | null>(null); // connected wallet id or null = manual
let isPaying = $state(false);
let payError = $state<string | null>(null);
```

### 3. Show connected wallet options below the address copy section
After the address/copy section, add:
```
{#if FeatureFlagService.isEnabled(FEATURE_FLAGS.CONNECTED_WALLETS) && $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.length > 0}
    <div class="divider text-xs">Or pay directly from</div>
    <div class="space-y-2">
        {#each $connectedWalletsStore.wallets as wallet (wallet.id)}
            <button
                class="btn btn-outline w-full min-h-[44px] justify-start gap-3"
                onclick={() => handlePayFromWallet(wallet.id)}
                disabled={isPaying}
            >
                <!-- wallet emoji -->
                <div class="text-left">
                    <div class="text-sm font-medium">{wallet.walletName}</div>
                    <div class="text-xs opacity-50">{wallet.address.slice(0,10)}...{wallet.address.slice(-4)}</div>
                </div>
                {#if selectedPayerWallet === wallet.id && isPaying}
                    <span class="loading loading-spinner loading-sm ml-auto"></span>
                {/if}
            </button>
        {/each}
    </div>
{/if}
```

### 4. Handle payment from wallet
```
async function handlePayFromWallet(walletId: string) {
    selectedPayerWallet = walletId;
    isPaying = true;
    payError = null;

    try {
        const handle = connectorRegistry.get(walletId);
        if (!handle?.evmSigner) throw new EVMSignerNotAvailableError(walletId);

        // Determine the payment method and construct transaction
        if (props.escrowDetails.paymentMethod === 'lbtc-liquid') {
            // For Liquid, send RBTC to the liquid address via evmSigner
            // ... similar to SendPaymentForm's connected wallet path
        } else {
            // For Lightning, note: direct Lightning payments from connected wallets aren't supported
            appStore.showErrorToast('Lightning payments from connected wallets are not currently supported. Please use the manual QR code option.');
            isPaying = false;
            return;
        }

        // On success, call onPaymentConfirmed
        props.onPaymentConfirmed();
    } catch (err) {
        payError = err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Payment failed';
        isPaying = false;
    }
}
```

### 5. Import appStore
```
import { appStore } from '$lib/stores/app.store';
```

### 6. Transaction construction for Liquid payments
For `lbtc-liquid`, the escrow address is a Liquid address. To pay from an EVM wallet:
```
// Construct RBTC transfer transaction to the escrow address
const chainId = 30; // RSK mainnet
const amountWei = BigInt(props.bid.amount); // amount is in sats
const txResult = await handle.evmSigner.sendTransaction({
    to: props.escrowDetails.address,
    value: amountWei * 10n ** 10n, // sats → wei (RBTC 18 decimals)
    chainId
});
```

## Defensive requirements
- Svelte 5 runes only: `$state()`, `$props()`, `$derived()` — no `$:` or `export let`
- Guard `connectorRegistry.get()` with null check
- Feature flag gate all additions
- Error handling with `appStore.showErrorToast()`
- Loading state prevents double-submit
- Keep all existing functionality untouched
- The manual address/QR path remains available for wallets without EVM signer support
- Lightning payments from connected wallets should show a clear error explaining why

## Output
