agents.prompt:
You are adding connected wallet support to `src/lib/components/wallet/BuySellForm.svelte`.

## Current State
BuySellForm is a buy/sell drawer that converts fiat ↔ crypto. It currently:
- Uses ONLY the built-in wallet (`$walletStore.rsk`, `$walletStore.bsc`) for balances
- Has `selectedCrypto` state (`'rbtc' | 'usdt-bsc'`)  
- Shows balance on each asset card (lines 329-367 in template)
- `setMaxAmount()` uses `rbtcBalance` / `usdtBalance` from built-in wallet
- `handleSubmit()` is a mock — sends no actual transaction

## What to Add

### 1. Source wallet selector (similar to SendPaymentForm pattern)
Add a "From" accordion at the top of the form (after tab bar, before asset cards) that lets the user choose:
- "BitTasker Wallet" (built-in, default)
- Connected wallets (under a "Connected" divider)

Pattern from SendPaymentForm lines 1985-2110:
```
<div class="collapse-arrow collapse...">
    <button>From: [selected source name + balance]</button>
    <div class="collapse-content">
        <button>BitTasker Wallet (built-in)</button>
        {#each connected wallets}
        <button>{wallet name + truncated address}</button>
        {/each}
    </div>
</div>
```

### 2. State
Add:
```
import { connectedWalletsStore } from '$lib/stores/connected-wallets.store';
import { connectorRegistry } from '$lib/services/external-wallet/connector-registry';
import { FeatureFlagService, FEATURE_FLAGS } from '$lib/services/kill-switch';

let selectedSource = $state<string>('builtin'); // 'builtin' or connected wallet id
let isConnectedWalletSource = $derived(selectedSource !== 'builtin');
```

### 3. Dynamic balance display
Modify `rbtcBalance` and `usdtBalance` derived values to use the selected source:
```
let rbtcBalance = $derived.by(() => {
    if (isConnectedWalletSource) {
        const w = $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.find(w => w.id === selectedSource);
        const raw = Number(w?.balances?.rbtc?.raw ?? 0);
        return (raw / 100_000_000).toFixed(6);
    }
    return $walletStore.rsk?.formattedBalance || '0.00';
});

let usdtBalance = $derived.by(() => {
    if (isConnectedWalletSource) {
        const w = $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.find(w => w.id === selectedSource);
        const raw = Number(w?.balances?.usdt?.raw ?? 0);
        return (raw / 1e18).toFixed(2);
    }
    return $walletStore.bsc?.formattedUsdtBalance || '0.00';
});
```

### 4. Update `setMaxAmount`
Use the same pattern — read from connected wallet when selected:
```
function setMaxAmount() {
    triggerHaptic(ImpactStyle.Light);
    const maxVal = isConnectedWalletSource
        ? (selectedCrypto === 'rbtc' 
            ? (() => { const w = $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.find(w => w.id === selectedSource); return String(Math.floor(Number(w?.balances?.rbtc?.raw ?? 0) / 100_000_000)); })()
            : (() => { const w = $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.find(w => w.id === selectedSource); return (Number(w?.balances?.usdt?.raw ?? 0) / 1e18).toString(); })())
        : (selectedCrypto === 'rbtc' ? parseFloat(rbtcBalance).toString() : usdtBalance);
    amount = maxVal;
    fetchQuoteForAmount(maxVal);
}
```

### 5. Template addition
Add the "From" accordion between the tab bar (line 325 `</div>`) and the "Digital Asset Selection" section (line 327 `<!-- Digital Asset Selection`):

```svelte
{#if FeatureFlagService.isEnabled(FEATURE_FLAGS.CONNECTED_WALLETS) && $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.length > 0}
    <div class="collapse-arrow border-primary bg-base-100 collapse rounded-lg border-2">
        <button type="button" class="collapse-title flex min-h-0 items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium"
            onclick={(e) => { const el = e.currentTarget.parentElement; el?.classList.toggle('collapse-open'); }}>
            <span class="text-base-content/60">From:</span>
            {#if selectedSource === 'builtin'}
                <span>BitTasker Wallet</span>
            {:else}
                {@const wallet = $connectedWalletsStore.wallets.find(w => w.id === selectedSource)}
                {#if wallet}
                    {#if wallet.walletType === 'metamask'}🦊
                    {:else if wallet.walletType === 'walletconnect'}🔗
                    {:else if wallet.walletType === 'trezor'}🔐
                    {:else if wallet.walletType === 'ledger'}💾
                    {/if}
                    <span>{wallet.walletName}</span>
                    <span class="text-base-content/50 ml-auto truncate text-xs">{wallet.address.slice(0,8)}...{wallet.address.slice(-4)}</span>
                {/if}
            {/if}
        </button>
        <div class="collapse-content px-2">
            <div class="space-y-1">
                <button class="...{selectedSource === 'builtin' ? 'bg-primary/10' : ''}..."
                    onclick={() => (selectedSource = 'builtin')}>
                    <img src="/images/chains/Bitcoin-Rootstock-logo.webp" class="h-5 w-5"/>
                    BitTasker Wallet
                </button>
                <div class="divider my-1 text-xs">Connected</div>
                {#each $connectedWalletsStore.wallets as wallet (wallet.id)}
                    <button class="...{selectedSource === wallet.id ? 'bg-primary/10' : ''}..."
                        onclick={() => (selectedSource = wallet.id)}>
                        {wallet type emoji}
                        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-left">
                            <div class="text-sm font-medium">{wallet.walletName}</div>
                            <div class="truncate text-xs opacity-50">{wallet.address.slice(0,10)}...{wallet.address.slice(-4)}</div>
                        </div>
                    </button>
                {/each}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{/if}
```

